# netsurf: a page with frames takes the local rebuild paths (patch 371)
# Generated 2026-11-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 370)
#
# The patch-370 census (r95c, 21 sites): after 370 routed style attribute
# changes locally, every one of rte's six then declined on "page has
# frames", and rte's and guardian's own batches did too. The local path
# (html_reconvert_local_change, patch 165) and the late-object relayout
# (html_relayout_object_local, WS-C item 2B) refused any change on a page
# holding a single iframe record. Two things a frame needs are real; the
# rest of the page is not theirs:
#
#  1. Nothing may free a frame's box. Its record (c->iframe, which
#     browser_window_recalculate_iframes walks -- cur->box->node -- on
#     every reformat) and its window (window->box) point at it. The local
#     paths already declined on b->iframe (the window), but a record can
#     have no window yet or ever: a same-origin frame a script made,
#     frames past SCRIPT_FRAMES_MAX. box_iframe marks each box it makes a
#     record for IFRAME, so the checks now test HTML_RL_FRAME (window or
#     flag), and the line path's old-content test looks below the line's
#     top level too (a frame in an inline-block whose removal left the
#     new content plain). No local path builds a frame: the new-content
#     tag lists hold no iframe.
#  2. Nothing may move a frame's box without the full layout's
#     descendant pass, which places its window at it (layout.c,
#     browser_window_set_position). Already so: layout_relayout_core
#     declines on a frame after the change (lr_subtree_unsafe, "positioned
#     box or iframe after it") and the page is laid out whole -- the box
#     tree is still rebuilt locally, the bulk of a full reconvert's cost
#     (unit 362's measurement). A frame's own box is never laid out by a
#     local path.
#
# Gate: JS-frames-local (eleven steps above and below a frame; a
# script-made frame appended, then removed; a frame removed inside an
# inline-block) renders row for row as CSS-frames-local-ref, the same
# steps at parse time; 7 or more of its changes rebuilt locally, the two
# frame removals still the full rebuild, and no "page has frames" line.
#
